WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.952 --> 00:00:03.535
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:08.531
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:11.460
- [Kelly] I love this whole look.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.293
- Oh my God, thank you.

00:00:12.293 --> 00:00:14.460
- Y'all Look like you're about
to make a real rad video.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.630
I'm just saying right now.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.463
- Yes, yes.

00:00:16.463 --> 00:00:17.296
- Have you ever met Seal?
Have y'all ever met?

00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:18.129
- No.

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:19.380
= No, we haven't had the pleasure.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.880
- Well, now you have. You're welcome.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:21.713
- So nice to meet you.

00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:22.546
- Nice to meet you too.

00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:23.379
- Legend.

00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:24.212
- Aw, thank you.

00:00:24.212 --> 00:00:26.490
- So wait, we all made
it through the pandemic

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.720
and we weren't able to do live shows.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.830
We weren't able to be out there.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.491
That was kind of hard
for a lot of us artists.

00:00:30.491 --> 00:00:33.660
But you're out there now, so
what's your favorite thing

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.920
since you've been back out on the road?

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.930
Favorite city, favorite
thing, favorite feeling?

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.390
- Just being with the
audience. A real audience.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.940
I just did a Jingle Ball
iHeart Radio Arena tour.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.310
I did all 10 shows in the
U.S. and it was so cool.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.620
Just night after night, arena after arena

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:48.660
and just like feeling the crowd.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.493
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:49.493 --> 00:00:50.943
- And not being home through Zoom.

00:00:52.155 --> 00:00:53.460
And you know, even now with
everybody here, it's great.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.530
- I know you forget like you feed off

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.970
that energy as a performer.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:57.803
- Yeah.

00:00:57.803 --> 00:00:59.130
- And we really got to
know that when you're like

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.750
all of a sudden doing like private shows

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.000
or any kind of show, like from a camera.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.110
- Yes. It was just-

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:04.943
- [Kelly] Weird.

00:01:04.943 --> 00:01:06.307
- It is weird. Because you're just like,

00:01:06.307 --> 00:01:08.250
"okay, I am stuck at home".

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.083
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.410
- And how am I gonna connect?

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.089
- [Kelly] Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:12.089 --> 00:01:12.922
And that's, it's a lot harder to do.

00:01:12.922 --> 00:01:15.900
So what things do you have
to do before or after shows?

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.610
Do you have any like rituals or anything?

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.850
- Oh man, this is tough
because I do a lot of stuff

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.320
with a lot of people all the time.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.410
But I always have Ava time carved out-

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.243
- [Kelly] Oh right before?

00:01:26.243 --> 00:01:27.690
- on my schedule right before I perform.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:28.712
- Yeah.

00:01:28.712 --> 00:01:29.670
- So like, everyone's putting my wires on

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.440
and my mic pack and everything.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.420
And then I have 15 minutes to myself

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.680
and I just kind of meditate.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.061
Close my eyes and just like,

00:01:36.061 --> 00:01:38.700
remember, you know, my
name, what I'm singing.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.533
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:39.533 --> 00:01:40.560
- Stuff like that. (laughs)

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.570
- I literally have 15 minutes carved out

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.700
before I go on stage where
I have my alone time.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:45.570
That's the same thing.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:46.920
- Really? Isn't it the best though?

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.210
- Because everybody's always around you.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.440
Even if you love them, you're just like

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.690
I just need a minute to
breathe before I get out there.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.213
- Yes. And I'm the type
of person where I do like,

00:01:55.744 --> 00:01:58.560
I really thrive through
the chaos. I love it.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.960
I feel like my house
is in the sky sometimes

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.910
because I'm barely even home
in L.A., when I'm in L.A..

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.550
- [Kelly] Yeah. Seat three A. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.030
- So I'm actually more comfortable

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.520
on tour lately, which is weird, but-

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.780
- That's a young thing. That was me too.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.710
- But I still need...

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.577
No, no, no, but I still need my Ava time.

00:02:13.577 --> 00:02:14.410
- Absolutely.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.660
- I still need that carved in.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.800
- Do you have any like thing you have

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.140
to do before you go on stage or after?

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.210
- Just balance. I just try and stay-

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.260
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.730
- Focused and it varies.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.875
Sometimes there are people,
I like people around.

00:02:26.875 --> 00:02:27.930
Sometimes I like being
by myself, but as long

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:31.680
as I have that moment that
where I can kind of connect

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.610
with that inner self and
just establish some kind

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.830
of balance, it could,
you know, 10-15 minutes

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:38.663
before I'm fine.

00:02:38.663 --> 00:02:40.630
- I think that you're like
a naturally chill person.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:41.516
[Seal] I'm not.

00:02:41.516 --> 00:02:42.441
- I think people that are ADHD

00:02:42.441 --> 00:02:43.274
(Seal laughs)

00:02:43.274 --> 00:02:44.107
- [Ava] You sound so chill.

00:02:44.107 --> 00:02:45.180
- You sound very chill.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.830
And I'm like, I'm too ADHD.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.725
So that's why I have
to carve out the time.

00:02:48.725 --> 00:02:49.560
- I'm not chill.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.734
- Oh, okay. You are pretending
really well right now.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:52.705
- Yeah, I am.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.270
- I'm like, "What does he do?
Meditate? What should I do?"

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.538
- I know, give us some tips.

00:02:56.538 --> 00:02:57.371
- I know.

00:02:57.371 --> 00:02:58.650
I was like, I could definitely
use some of that help.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.060
But I wanna talk about your new album.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.670
This is the coolest title.
It's Diamonds and Dance Floors.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.230
So like why is that the title?

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.550
- Thank you.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:06.383
So Diamonds and Dance Floors

00:03:06.383 --> 00:03:09.390
was the first song on the album.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.223
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.520
- One of the first that
I wrote for the album.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.490
And at that time I didn't
have an album title.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.170
And it was called
Diamonds and Dance Floors,

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.003
the title track.

00:03:17.003 --> 00:03:19.087
And after I finished it, I was like,

00:03:19.087 --> 00:03:21.330
"why does this feel so right?"

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.730
Especially with like,
starting in the pandemic

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.770
I wanted to be on a dance floor.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.180
That song, the title track is talking

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.190
about like being in my
kitchen and living room

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.070
just dancing by myself wishing
I was feeling the rhythm

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.900
and just bodies next to me.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.733
And so...

00:03:34.733 --> 00:03:35.566
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:03:35.566 --> 00:03:38.036
- It just came about when I
wrote Diamonds and Dance Floors.

00:03:38.036 --> 00:03:41.360
- I heard, so what's the song
Million Dollar Baby about?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.730
- It's about coming out
stronger from a breakup I had.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.782
- I thought, I was like, a lot

00:03:45.782 --> 00:03:49.050
of people went through a
breakup during the pandemic.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.680
And it was a hard time already,
I feel like for a lot of us.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.840
But then going through that

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.450
and just being feeling more
isolated and more lonely.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.480
I think a lot of creatives
got to work in the studio.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.970
Because that's how we kind
of, that's our outlet, right?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.560
Is that kind of what
this album is for you?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.393
- Oh, for sure.

00:04:05.393 --> 00:04:07.350
I would always say I'm never talking

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.970
about my personal life.
I'm never gonna do it.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:09.803
I'm not gonna do it.

00:04:09.803 --> 00:04:11.610
I'm only gonna talk about how
I came up in the industry.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.380
I'm gonna talk about female
empowerment and that's it.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.080
And then I died inside. (laughs)

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:16.913
- Yeah.

00:04:16.913 --> 00:04:18.720
- And that was all I could write about.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:19.553
- Yeah.

00:04:19.553 --> 00:04:20.820
- That was all I could even-

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.400
- But unfortunately it's highly relatable-

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.447
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:04:24.447 --> 00:04:25.890
- Like people that can't write music.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.180
Like maybe that's how they get through.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.240
Even before I started writing,
that's how I could cope.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.073
- Oh yeah.

00:04:31.073 --> 00:04:31.906
- That's how I could connect.

00:04:31.906 --> 00:04:32.820
- No, I see things differently.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.150
Heartbreak is actually,
yes, it's bad and negative

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.440
but it's also a good thing.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.050
And I, because you
change, you grow stronger-

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:40.949
- [Kelly] You learn about yourself.

00:04:40.949 --> 00:04:44.370
- you learn about yourself.
You see life differently.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.980
You see people differently.
You appreciate things more.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.800
I don't know, it's, I came
out from the other side

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.026
like completely different.

00:04:52.026 --> 00:04:54.205
To the point where I'm just like,

00:04:54.205 --> 00:04:56.530
"do I get heartbroken again?"

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.990
(laughing) Just kidding.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:58.823
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:58.823 --> 00:04:59.656
- Don't worry, there's therapy for that.

00:04:59.656 --> 00:05:01.920
- I don't want to, I really
don't want to. But...

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.840
- It is amazing. I always make this joke.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.143
I only make good records
whenever sadness involved.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.200
It's hard to write,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.110
like, it is a lot harder to
write happy songs I feel like.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.850
When you're writing
about desperation or ache

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:18.420
or sadness or just some kind
of like thing to overcome,

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.000
it's just more appealing to me.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.140
- It's... (laughing)

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:22.973
- Well...

00:05:22.973 --> 00:05:25.050
- It's crazy. It just,
it hits differently,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.301
lyrics to me now.

00:05:26.301 --> 00:05:27.233
- [Kelly] Yeah I agree.
- For sure.

